hopwyn (0.3.1-0ppa1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * On GNOME, no permission dialog any more: not at startup, and not
    after a restart.
  * New "Share the clipboard" setting, off by default: text copied on
    one device can be pasted on your other paired devices.

 -- Dhivakar R (Dhiva-Labs) <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:45:48 +0530

hopwyn (0.3.0-0ppa1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Reconnects after a change of network: each device remembers where it
    last reached the other, and either one may start the connection.
  * Add computer shows this computer's address, to type on a device that
    can't find it on networks that hide devices from each other.
  * A device that keeps dropping the connection is shown as such and
    retried only now and then, instead of reconnecting in a loop.
  * The status card says when it is waiting for input sharing to be
    allowed, instead of "Ready".

 -- Dhivakar R (Dhiva-Labs) <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:24:13 +0530

hopwyn (0.2.0-0ppa1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Asks for input permissions only when needed, or once at startup, as
    you choose; works with the other computer offline.
  * Drag computers anywhere around the screen, with multi-monitor
    layouts and screens of different sizes.
  * Pairs with the Hopwyn Android app: use the phone as a trackpad and
    keyboard, or move the pointer onto the phone to control it.
  * Fixes: hidden permission dialogs, stalled edge capture, pairing
    announcements that weren't noticed.

 -- Dhivakar R (Dhiva-Labs) <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0530

hopwyn (0.1.0-0ppa1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First packaged developer preview: pair by comparing a code on both
    screens, up to four computers arranged by dragging, encrypted
    home-network link, Linux capture and injection through the desktop
    portals.

